//? Title: Reference counting: actual count mutations, cascading frees and cycle-held leaks
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A reference counter can reclaim an object as soon as its last incoming reference
disappears, but cycles can keep unreachable objects alive. The native simulation
counts every root and field, then records its actual LIFO zero-count cascade.
The original eight-object heap remains. Explicit self-cycle, cycle-tail and
duplicate-field controls distinguish actual reclaimed objects from all
unreachable unreclaimed garbage.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For each object v, initialize
$$ c(v)=\#\{\text{roots referencing }v\}+\#\{u\to v\text{ fields}\}. $$
\alttext(Reference count is the actual number of incoming root and object-field references.)
Zero-count objects have no remaining incoming ownership edge. Reclaiming one
removes each of its outgoing references, decrementing those targets and possibly
producing new zeros. Induction over this cascade preserves each surviving
object's actual incoming count. Duplicate roots and fields count separately; a
field release occurs once for every stored field.

An unreachable cycle has no zero-count member, so the cascade cannot start
inside it. Its outgoing references can also keep noncyclic descendants alive:
leaked means every unreachable unreclaimed object, not only vertices that belong
to a cycle. A separate canonical root-reachability traversal supplies that
classification. Complete graph validation prevents out-of-range roots or
unreachable fields from corrupting the count arrays. Simulation time/storage is
linear in objects, fields and roots, plus optional actual event histories.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/reference_counting_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto graph = a::reference_count_chain(3);
    auto t = a::reference_counting_trace(graph);
    std::print("\n| actual event kind (root0,field1,free2,release3) | actual source | actual target | count " "before | count after | actual pending zeros |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", int(e.kind), e.source,
                   e.target, e.before, e.after, e.pending);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual initial incoming counts\n{}", t.result.refcount));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual LIFO cascade free order\n{}", t.freed_order));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual unreachable unreclaimed ids\n{}", t.result.leaked));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/reference_counting_tiny.svg");
}
```
