> API and interpretation

This is a checked graph simulation, not C++ shared_ptr or an allocator. Initial
refcount and final_counts are distinct owned fields. Actual mutation history
records count changes and real pending-stack length; it does not regenerate a
cascade. The underlying ObjectGraph requires complete nonnegative dense ids;
negative/null references are omitted rather than stored. The original graph size
metadata is unused. Selected-operation counters exclude the separate complete
validator and canonical reachability traversal, so they are not all CPU
instructions, byte budgets or wall-clock costs.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

